content.text:
Here's what a real rich `toolUseResult` looks like for a Read tool call:

```json
{
  "toolUseResult": {
    "type": "text",
    "file": {
      "filePath": "/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli/.../manual_commit_attribution.go",
      "content": "package strategy\nimport ...",  // full file content!
      "numLines": 441,
      "startLine": 1,
      "totalLines": 441
    }
  },
  "tool_result_block": {
    "tool_use_id": "REDACTED",
    "content": "     1→package strategy\n     2→\n..."  // line-numbered view
  }
}
```

So the compact converter currently takes only `toolUseResult.stdout` (which doesn't exist here — this is the `file` shape, not the Bash `stdout`/`stderr` shape). The `toolUseResult.stdout` enrichment in `compact.go:287-303` **only fires for Bash-style results**. For Read tool results with `file` shape, the compact converter falls through to the `tool_result.content` block — that line-numbered text dump of the file.

The native `ClaudeCodeParser` extracts `file.filePath` and `file.numLines` and puts them on `ToolCallResult.file`, which the frontend uses to show "Read manual_commit_attribution.go (441 lines)" instead of dumping 441 lines of raw text.

This is the actual information loss: **15-25 Read tool calls per session lose their structured file metadata** and become raw text blobs in the compact format.

